# Source: Ventrax AV4 report. Acceptance specification; execution is verified separately.
Feature: Support tickets, technical visits and service ratings

  Scenario: Create a support ticket for an authorized meter
    Given an authenticated user has permission to create tickets for meter A
    When the user submits a valid ticket with a subject and description
    Then Support registers the ticket and links it to meter A

  Scenario: Reject a ticket for an unauthorized meter
    Given a subuser has no ticket permission for meter B
    When the subuser attempts to create or access a ticket for meter B
    Then Support denies the operation without disclosing the protected resource

  Scenario: Add a written reply and photograph
    Given an authorized user has an open support ticket
    When the user submits a valid written reply and an allowed photograph
    Then Support preserves the reply and attachment in the ticket history

  Scenario: Request a technical visit without advance payment
    Given a ticket remains unresolved and the user has visit permission
    When the user requests a visit and provides an availability interval
    Then Support creates a linked visit without requiring prior payment

  Scenario: Automatically assign an accredited technician
    Given a visit is requested and an accredited technician is available
    When the assignment policy executes
    Then Support records the assigned technician and the corresponding visit state

  Scenario: Restrict technician administration to SuperAdmin
    Given an authenticated user does not have SuperAdmin role
    When the user attempts to modify technician accreditation
    Then Support denies the operation

  Scenario: Complete a technical visit
    Given a technical visit is in progress
    When the final diagnosis and cost are recorded
    Then Support completes the visit and makes its finalization information available to Billing

  Scenario: Close and rate completed attention
    Given a support ticket is resolved and belongs to the principal user
    When the principal user confirms its closure and submits a valid rating
    Then Support records the closed status and preserves the service rating
